The Commissioner may, by notice in writing, require the trustees of a registered pension fund or pension scheme and an employer who contributes to any such fund to furnish him within a reasonable time, not being less than thirty days from the date of service of such notice, with a return containing–
  (a) the name and place of residence of every person in receipt of any payment made under the regulations of such fund or scheme;
  (b) the amount and nature of any such payment;
  (c) a copy of the accounts of any such fund or scheme up to the last date prior to such notice to which such accounts have been made up; and
